 "how_they_run_it": "TextOpTracker/scripts/deploy_mujoco.py (sim2sim): MuJoCo g1_act.xml with torque motors, sim dt 0.002, control_decimation 10 (=50 Hz; NOT the 0.005x4 used in training). Init: qpos joints = motion joint_pos[0] remapped to MuJoCo order, root pos/quat = motion pelvis pose at frame 0. Every sim step tau = kp*(q_target - q) - kd*dq (target dq = 0), then mj_step. Every 10th step: build the 431-dim obs [cmd 290 | anchor_pos_b 15 | anchor_ori_b 30 | proj_grav 3 | base_lin_vel 3 | base_ang_vel 3 | q-default 29 | dq 29 | last_action 29] using the robot's simulated pelvis body pose and the motion frames t..t+4 (clamped), run ONNX, q_target = action[isaaclab_to_mujoco]*scale + default, advance motion index by 1; stops at end of motion. Real robot (C++ ROS2, textop_onnx_controller.cpp) uses the same layout but zeroes anchor_pos_b, uses IMU quat for anchor orientation and aligns the reference yaw/xy to the robot at t=0 (observation_computer.cpp:637-708).",
